  "notes": "Transcribed via pdftotext -layout from the ORC Speed Guide PDF (J/70 ONE DESIGN, Sail No USA 1, Issued 4/30/2012, VPP 2011 1.02, (c) Offshore Racing Congress 2011). The guide prints three polar tables per TWS: 'Best Performance' (combined optimum of jib and asymmetric spinnaker), 'Jib', and 'Asymmetric Spinnaker on Centerline'. Only the two sail-specific tables (Jib, Asymmetric Spinnaker on CL) are included here; the 'Best Performance' table is the per-angle max of these two and was omitted as redundant. Column mapping: guide's BTV -> bsKt, VMG -> vmgKt, Heel -> heelDeg. Rows marked '(b)' in the guide (optimal upwind VMG angle) are kind=vmgUp; rows marked '(r)' (optimal downwind VMG angle) are kind=vmgDn; all other printed TWA rows are kind=angle. The Jib table's '(r)' row is the VMG-optimal angle for jib-only sailing (close to 180 deg, not a true reaching/running sail choice) as printed by the guide. AWS, AWA, Reef, and Flat columns from the guide were not carried into this file."
